WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.975
Book Two, Proposition Five.

2
00:00:01.975 --> 00:00:14.589
If a segment be cut into equal and unequal segments, the rectangle contained by the unequal segments of the whole together with the square on the segment between the points of section is equal to the square on the half.

3
00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:19.370
Let the segment A B be cut into equal segments at C and into unequal segments at D.

4
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:27.968
On the half C B, describe the square C E F B by One Forty-Six, and join the diagonal B E.

5
00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:43.680
Through D, draw D G parallel to C E or B F by One Thirty-One, meeting B E at H; through H, draw K M parallel to A B or E F; and through A, draw A K parallel to C L or B M.

6
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.124
By One Forty-Three, the complement C H equals the complement H F.

7
00:00:49.124 --> 00:00:54.225
Adding the square D M to each, the whole C M equals the whole D F.

8
00:00:54.225 --> 00:01:02.185
And since A C equals C B, parallelogram A L equals C M by One Thirty-Six, and therefore A L equals D F.

9
00:01:02.185 --> 00:01:07.441
Adding C H to each, the whole rectangle A H equals the gnomon N O P.

10
00:01:07.441 --> 00:01:18.029
Because D H equals D B, A H is the rectangle contained by A D and D B, so the gnomon N O P equals the rectangle contained by A D and D B.

11
00:01:18.029 --> 00:01:21.816
Now add L G, which is the square on C D, to each.

12
00:01:21.816 --> 00:01:27.613
Together, the gnomon N O P and L G compose the whole square C E F B on C B.

13
00:01:27.613 --> 00:01:35.882
Therefore, the rectangle contained by A D and D B together with the square on C D equals the square on C B.

14
00:01:35.882 --> 00:01:37.660
Which was to be proved.

15
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:49.163
Proposition Two Five is the geometric engine for completing the square and the difference of two squares: x y plus the square of a over two minus y equals the square of a over two.

16
00:01:49.163 --> 00:02:04.987
By folding the rectangle A H into the L-shaped gnomon N O P inside the square on the half, Euclid solves the quadratic equation a x minus x squared equals b squared, and proves that among all rectangles of a given perimeter, the square has the maximum area.

17
00:02:04.987 --> 00:02:16.440
